SWEET CPUSTAT row cap fix (patch 0175, AP-173, B-A6): pid 1 and every process named in sweetcpuwatch print their 'CPUSTAT p' row on every full sample, whatever their CPU and outside the CS_MAX_LINES 200 cap; rows the cap drops are counted on 'CPUSTAT truncated N rows', processes whose task_info fails on 'CPUSTAT skipped N procs' (a watched one also on 'CPUSTAT p <pid> <name> task_info failed'); the parsed list is printed once ('CPUSTAT watching N names from "..."'); a sweetcpuwatch name that is empty, too long or over the limit, or a list that gives no name, is a 'SWEET GAP: CPUSTAT' line instead of being dropped silently (review cpustat-cap-r1 F2/F3). CS_WATCH_MAX 4 -> 8, watch buffer 128 -> 256 B, default watch list adds launchd,mediaserverd. The sample body moves into cs_sample() and the list parse into cs_parse_watch() (host test tools/test_cpustat_c.py compiles them). Read-only diagnostics, no register access. Not run on hardware.

