  * Boot-arg sweetcpustat=N (seconds, default 60, 0 = off). Every N seconds one kernel thread prints
  *   CPUSTAT --- up <ms> ms | ufs ios <n> cmds <n> KiB <n> busy <ms> lockwait <ms> maxcmd <us> (cumulative since boot)
  *   CPUSTAT p <pid> <name> user <ms> sys <ms>        (cumulative CPU of every process with >= 100 ms)
- * and every 5 s it checks the processes named in boot-arg sweetcpuwatch (default
- * "com.apple.migrationpluginwrapper,com.apple.datamigrator") and prints
+ *   CPUSTAT truncated <n> rows (cap <CS_MAX_LINES>; watched rows not capped)   (only when rows were dropped)
+ * Patch 0175 (AP-173): pid 1 and every process named in sweetcpuwatch get their CPUSTAT p row on every full sample,
+ * whatever their CPU and outside the CS_MAX_LINES cap; the cap now counts and reports what it drops, and a process
+ * whose task_info fails is counted on a "CPUSTAT skipped" line (a watched one also gets "CPUSTAT p <pid> <name> task_info
+ * failed"). The parsed watch list is printed once ("CPUSTAT watching N names"); a name that does not fit, or an empty list,
+ * is a SWEET GAP line.
+ * Every 5 s it checks the processes named in boot-arg sweetcpuwatch (default
+ * "com.apple.migrationpluginwrapper,com.apple.datamigrator,launchd,mediaserverd", at most CS_WATCH_MAX names) and prints
  *   CPUSTAT watch <name> live <n> at <ms> ms           (only when the count of live processes with that name changes)
  * so the end of the migration is logged to 5 s. Deltas between two samples are computed on the host.
  * UFS counters are kept by sweet_ufs_strategy (sweet_ufs.c) under its lock; reads here are unlocked (diagnostic only).
